  "term": "levitation",
  "definition": "In this historical source, levitation refers to a delusional feeling that one’s body is rising or floating, linked to abnormal bodily and muscular sensations. It is described as occurring in certain forms of paralysis and hysterical insanity as part of disturbed body awareness.",
